│                          │ many random restarts of the sampled greedy (each with different random decisions) and     │
│                          │ keep the best schedule found, since greedy is stochastic and variance across restarts is  │
│                          │ high; (2) apply a 2-opt style local search afterward — try moving each transaction to a   │
│                          │ different position (insertion neighborhood) and accept improvements — to fix greedy's     │
│                          │ ordering mistakes. Evaluating candidates with `get_opt_seq_cost` keeps decisions tied to  │
│                          │ actual makespan, not heuristics.                                                          │
