│ patch_name               │ multi_restart_greedy_plus_swap_local_search                                               │
│ patch_description        │ Improvement strategy:                                                                     │
│                          │ 1. Replace the single random-start sampled greedy with multiple restarts. For each        │
│                          │ restart, at each step we evaluate every remaining transaction by the actual               │
│                          │ partial-schedule cost (`workload.get_opt_seq_cost`), which directly measures makespan     │
│                          │ contribution rather than a heuristic like transaction length.                             │
│                          │ 2. Vary starting transactions across restarts to explore different greedy basins, keeping │
│                          │ the best schedule found.                                                                  │
│                          │ 3. Add a swap-based local search: repeatedly try swapping adjacent (and later all)        │
│                          │ transaction pairs; keep a swap if it lowers the total makespan. This escapes local optima │
│                          │ of pure greedy.                                                                           │
│                          │ 4. A time budget keeps runtime bounded while maximizing improvement quality.              │
│                          │                                                                                           │
│                          │ This leads to better schedules because the greedy uses the true objective (incremental    │
│                          │ makespan) for evaluation, multiple restarts diversify search, and the local search        │
│                          │ polishes the result — directly lowering the makespan metric while keeping schedules valid │
│                          │ (permutations of all transactions).                                                       │
