│ Field                    │ Value                                                                                     │
├──────────────────────────┼───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┤
│ patch_type               │ diff                                                                                      │
│ patch_name               │ insertion_local_search_and_or GRASP improvements                                          │
│ patch_description        │ The current local search only considers adjacent swaps, which limits its ability to       │
│                          │ escape local optima — a transaction that would be much better placed far earlier or later │
│                          │ in the sequence is never moved more than one position at a time, and single-pass swaps    │
│                          │ converge quickly to a poor local minimum. My edit extends the local search with (1)       │
│                          │ insertion moves (remove a transaction from its position and try reinserting it at every   │
│                          │ other position), which are strictly more powerful than adjacent swaps and known to be     │
│                          │ effective for sequencing problems, and (2) an occasional random-restart perturbation      │
│                          │ (ruin-and-recreate style): if a GRASP run fails to improve the best solution, perturb the │
│                          │ best sequence by shuffling a random contiguous segment and re-optimizing with local       │
│                          │ search. This diversifies the search without extra greedy-construction cost (which is the  │
│                          │ expensive part since each candidate evaluation calls get_opt_seq_cost). Since all moves   │
│                          │ are evaluated on the true makespan, any accepted move is guaranteed to improve or         │
│                          │ maintain the real objective. This combination of stronger local moves plus perturbation   │
│                          │ restarts should reliably lower makespan relative to the current adjacent-swap-only        │
│                          │ scheme.                                                                                   │
