│ patch_type               │ diff                                                                                      │
│ patch_name               │ greedy_plus_2opt_swap_local_search                                                        │
│ patch_description        │ The current program builds a greedy schedule from each starting transaction. Greedy       │
│                          │ construction alone is myopic — it cannot repair ordering mistakes made early. A classic   │
│                          │ improvement is to follow each greedy construction with a local search: repeatedly try     │
│                          │ swapping pairs of transactions in the sequence (prioritizing swaps of nearby positions    │
│                          │ and swaps involving conflicting transactions, since makespan only changes when dependency │
│                          │ order of conflicting txns changes), accepting any swap that reduces makespan. Iterating   │
│                          │ this until no improving swap exists typically shaves significant makespan off greedy      │
│                          │ solutions. We keep multiple restarts (one per starting transaction plus randomized        │
│                          │ restarts) and apply local search to each, returning the best. This directly minimizes the │
│                          │ true objective (evaluated via get_opt_seq_cost) rather than heuristics, which the prompt  │
│                          │ warns against.                                                                            │
│ num_applied              │ 3                                                                                         │
