│ patch_type               │ diff                                                                                      │
│ patch_name               │ insertion_swap_local_search                                                               │
│ patch_description        │ The recommendation suggests combining insertion moves (best performing, 277.00) with      │
│                          │ pairwise-swap moves (296.00) in a hybrid neighborhood. Adjacent-swap-only local search    │
│                          │ can get stuck: an insertion move relocates a transaction to any position (not just ±1),   │
│                          │ unlocking improvements swaps cannot reach, while swaps reorder without                    │
│                          │ removing/reinserting. I replace the adjacent-swap-only local search with a hybrid that    │
│                          │ does a full best-insertion sweep followed by a full adjacent-swap sweep each pass,        │
│                          │ iterating until no improvement. This dominates the previous neighborhood (adjacent swaps  │
│                          │ are a subset of insertion+swap reach) at modest extra cost, since each candidate move is  │
│                          │ evaluated with the true makespan via `get_opt_seq_cost`.                                  │
