│ patch_description        │ Key parameters in the current approach: fixed 20 restarts of greedy sampling              │
│                          │ (num_samples=6, sample_rate=0.95) plus one full 2-opt style swap/reinsertion local        │
│                          │ search. The new approach replaces fixed iteration counts with a wall-clock time budget    │
│                          │ (~2.5s per workload): run randomized greedy restarts continuously, and after each greedy  │
│                          │ solution apply first-improvement pairwise-swap local search (cheaper than full            │
│                          │ best-improvement VNS). Track best globally. Using more greedy restarts with smaller       │
│                          │ sample counts and a cheaper local search per restart yields more diverse candidates       │
│                          │ within the budget, which empirically lowers makespan. Also defensively import time both   │
│                          │ at module level and inside the function to avoid NameError failures.                      │
