│ patch_description        │ Keep `import time` guaranteed at module level. Improve the search: (1) greedy             │
│                          │ construction as before, (2) local search alternating best-improvement insertion and       │
│                          │ adjacent/swap moves using a cached-cost delta evaluation where possible, (3) restarts     │
│                          │ from perturbed best with time budget check so all three workloads get their share of      │
│                          │ time. Key changes: fix the buggy insertion bookkeeping in the prior version (the best_j   │
│                          │ logic was broken), use both insertion and swap neighborhoods, and restart with            │
│                          │ double-bridge-style perturbation when stalled, always tracking global best. This yields   │
│                          │ lower makespans within the time budget.                                                   │
