│ patch_type               │ diff                                                                                      │
│ patch_name               │ hybrid_insertion_swap_search                                                              │
│ patch_description        │ The recommendation suggests interleaving a full pairwise-swap sweep with the              │
│                          │ insertion-based local search. Insertion moves (relocating a transaction to a different    │
│                          │ position) and adjacent/arbitrary swap moves (exchanging two transactions' positions)      │
│                          │ explore different neighborhoods of the schedule space; combining them within the proven   │
│                          │ restart/time-budget structure covers both move classes. Step-by-step reasoning: (1) the   │
│                          │ greedy construction gives a decent starting schedule; (2) insertion sweeps already        │
│                          │ improve it; (3) some local optima of the insertion neighborhood can only be escaped by    │
│                          │ swap moves (and vice versa), so alternating sweeps within each local search round         │
│                          │ converges to better minima; (4) the cost cache via get_opt_seq_cost ensures the same safe │
│                          │ API is used, no new API risk. We modify local_search_insertion to perform one insertion   │
│                          │ pass followed by one full pairwise-swap pass per round, keeping the existing              │
│                          │ 20-restart/100-second outer structure intact.                                             │
