│ patch_name               │ greedy_multistart_swap_reinsert                                                           │
│ patch_description        │ Combines the two best-performing approaches: (1) multi-restart randomized greedy          │
│                          │ construction that samples actual incremental makespan via `get_opt_seq_cost` when         │
│                          │ choosing the next transaction, and (2) a local search phase using full pairwise swaps     │
│                          │ plus reinsertion moves that continues until no improvement is found. Compared to the      │
│                          │ prior best, we additionally apply the local search to the top-3 greedy candidates (not    │
│                          │ just the single best), which increases diversity of starting points for the improvement   │
│                          │ phase and empirically escapes poor local minima. The greedy uses sample_rate ~0.95 with 6 │
│                          │ samples per step to balance exploration and cost-evaluation budget. Reasoning             │
│                          │ step-by-step: greedy construction alone leaves transactions misplaced; pairwise swaps fix │
│                          │ ordering mistakes while reinsertion moves fix position mistakes; running improvement on   │
│                          │ multiple greedy seeds yields a better final makespan while keeping the same input/output  │
│                          │ interface.                                                                                │
