│ patch_type               │ diff                                                                                      │
│ patch_name               │ insertion_swap_hybrid_local_search                                                        │
│ patch_description        │ The insertion-based annealing program scored 3412.97 (makespan 292) while the pure        │
│                          │ swap-based program scored 3401.36 (293). Insertion (relocate) and swap explore different  │
│                          │ neighborhoods, and neither dominates. The recommendation is to interleave both: after     │
│                          │ each best-improvement swap sweep, run a full pairwise insertion sweep, alternating move   │
│                          │ types within the same local search so the search can escape local optima of one           │
│                          │ neighborhood class. Both use the proven cost cache (`eval_cost`) and the same             │
│                          │ `get_opt_seq_cost` API, so there's no new API risk. We keep the existing greedy restarts  │
│                          │ structure (deterministic starts for each transaction, then random) which previously       │
│                          │ validated well, and add the insertion sweep with best-improvement acceptance (no          │
│                          │ annealing noise, since the deterministic sweep structure was already reliable). Replacing │
│                          │ the spans-based swap with a full O(n²) swap sweep plus a full O(n²) insertion sweep per   │
│                          │ iteration gives broader coverage; the cost cache makes repeated evaluations cheap.        │
