│ patch_name               │ cost_cache_and_swap_sweep                                                                 │
│ patch_description        │ Two improvements: (1) add a memoization cache around `get_opt_seq_cost` so the annealing  │
│                          │ search, which repeatedly re-evaluates similar sequences, avoids redundant expensive       │
│                          │ evaluations — this dramatically increases the number of search iterations within the time │
│                          │ budget; (2) add a quick best-improvement swap sweep immediately after greedy construction │
│                          │ so the deep insertion search starts from a swap-polished solution. Swap moves (exchanging │
│                          │ two transaction positions) are complementary to insertions and cheap to scan, and greedy  │
│                          │ output typically contains swap-improvable disorder.                                       │
