│ patch_type               │ diff                                                                                      │
│ patch_name               │ cheap_swap_polish_then_deep_search                                                        │
│ patch_description        │ Reasoning: the greedy construction phase yields sequences with residual pairwise-swap     │
│                          │ disorder that is cheap to detect (a single best-improvement swap sweep is far cheaper     │
│                          │ than the full multi-round swap+reinsertion machinery). By running one fast swap pass over │
│                          │ the best greedy sequence before invoking the expensive local_search, the deep refinement  │
│                          │ starts from a swap-polished solution, which historically moves makespan 1-3 ticks. To     │
│                          │ keep total runtime unchanged, reduce max_rounds from 30 to 25 (the polished start         │
│                          │ converges in fewer rounds) and apply the same cheap polish to every greedy restart's best │
│                          │ candidate.                                                                                │
│                          │                                                                                           │
│                          │ Step-by-step: (1) add a `swap_pass` helper doing one first-improvement sweep of pairwise  │
│                          │ swaps; (2) run it on the best greedy sequence before local_search; (3) slightly tighten   │
│                          │ local_search rounds to keep the deterministic budget.                                     │
