│ patch_description        │ Inspired by the greedy cost-sampling construction and insertion local search from prior   │
│                          │ programs, this version implements a fundamentally different pipeline: (1) a randomized    │
│                          │ *regret-style* greedy that, instead of picking the single best next transaction, samples  │
│                          │ several candidates and picks one weighted toward low incremental cost, producing more     │
│                          │ diverse starting solutions; (2) a hybrid local search alternating **swap moves**          │
│                          │ (exchange two transaction positions — a move type prior programs never used, which        │
│                          │ explores a different neighborhood than insertion) with **insertion moves**; (3) a         │
│                          │ late-acceptance/annealing acceptance criterion allowing occasional uphill moves to escape │
│                          │ local optima, then a final greedy best-improvement polish. The 100s time budget is kept,  │
│                          │ with restarts.                                                                            │
