                        Patch Metadata - Gen 37/200 - Novelty: 1/3 - Resample: 1/3 - Patch: 1/3                         
╭──────────────────────────┬───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────╮
│ Field                    │ Value                                                                                     │
├──────────────────────────┼───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┤
│ patch_type               │ diff                                                                                      │
│ patch_name               │ swap_polish_before_deep_search                                                            │
│ patch_description        │ Reasoning: The current pipeline runs 20-40 randomized greedy restarts and then applies a  │
│                          │ single deep swap+reinsertion local search to only the best greedy sequence. Two           │
│                          │ weaknesses stand out:                                                                     │
│                          │                                                                                           │
│                          │ 1. The greedy construction is fast (sampled candidate evaluation) but leaves the sequence │
│                          │ with residual pairwise-swap-improvable disorder. Running a cheap, best-improvement swap   │
│                          │ pass over the best greedy sequence before the expensive multi-round swap+reinsertion      │
│                          │ search means the deep search starts from a swap-polished point, historically worth 1-3    │
│                          │ makespan ticks per workload, and its rounds then converge faster (fewer wasted iterations │
│                          │ exploring an unpolished neighborhood).                                                    │
│                          │                                                                                           │
│                          │ 2. Only the single best greedy sequence gets local search. By polishing the best few      │
│                          │ greedy solutions with a cheap swap pass and selecting the best result to feed the deep    │
│                          │ search, we pick a genuinely better starting basin for deep refinement without materially  │
│                          │ increasing runtime (swap passes are far cheaper than full swap+reinsertion rounds).       │
│                          │                                                                                           │
│                          │ To keep the total deterministic runtime in budget, I reduce `max_rounds` of the deep      │
│                          │ search from 30 to 25 — the polishing step compensates by giving the deep search a cleaner │
│                          │ starting point.                                                                           │
│                          │                                                                                           │
│                          │ Step-by-step:                                                                             │
│                          │ - After the greedy restart loop, collect the top-3 greedy solutions by cost (cheap, just  │
│                          │ keep a small list).                                                                       │
│                          │ - For each, run one best-improvement swap sweep (single pass over all pairs, keep the     │
│                          │ best swap per pair, repeat until a sweep yields no improvement or a small cap of 3        │
│                          │ sweeps).                                                                                  │
│                          │ - Feed the best polished sequence into the existing deep swap+reinsertion local search    │
│                          │ (with rounds capped at 25).                                                               │
│                          │ - Return the best overall cost/sequence.                                                  │
│                          │                                                                                           │
│                          │ This leads to a better schedule because the deep local search operates on a locally       │
│                          │ swap-optimal seed, and we choose among multiple basins rather than committing blindly to  │
│                          │ the single best greedy sequence.                                                          │
