│ patch_description        │ The current best program (273 makespan) uses randomized greedy restarts (6 samples, 0.95  │
│                          │ rate) followed by deep local search. The recommendation is to tune the greedy exploration │
│                          │ parameters per restart. I keep the winning true-cost greedy + swap/reinsertion local      │
│                          │ search, but: (1) add a cost cache keyed on tuple sequences to avoid recomputing identical │
│                          │ candidates, (2) schedule `sample_rate` from 0.95 down to 0.85 and `num_samples` from 6 up │
│                          │ to 10 across restarts — early restarts exploit the greedy signal (confirmed productive at │
│                          │ 0.95/6), later restarts diversify, (3) keep the top-3 greedy seeds and run the expensive  │
│                          │ deep local search on the best one, and (4) run greedy restarts under an overall time      │
│                          │ budget so no time is wasted. This is a low-risk parameter mutation on top of the proven   │
│                          │ structure, which should find at least as good a local optimum and likely better ones      │
│                          │ through diversified late restarts.                                                        │
