│ patch_name               │ or_opt_local_search                                                                       │
│ patch_description        │ The current local search uses insertion and swap moves. A classic improvement for         │
│                          │ sequencing problems is adding an Or-opt move: move a segment of 2-3 consecutive           │
│                          │ transactions to another position (possibly reversed). Segments of interacting             │
│                          │ transactions often need to move together — single-element insertion cannot reach these    │
│                          │ local optima in one move. Adding Or-opt as a third neighborhood in the random move        │
│                          │ sampling increases neighborhood coverage per round without extra rounds, and since cost   │
│                          │ evaluation is cached, repeated evaluations stay cheap. I sample segment moves with ~20%   │
│                          │ probability, keeping insertion and swap as dominant moves. This should escape a different │
│                          │ class of local minima and reduce makespan further.                                        │
│ num_applied              │ 2                                                                                         │
